1
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:18,680
Is there anyone who doesn’t know about those great friends Harry, Hermione and Ron in the Harry Potter books?

2
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:29,500
JK Rowling’s stories are world famous and part of their success is because of the friendship between those three main characters.

3
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:34,840
But there are many examples of great friends in literature.

4
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:37,326
Let’s look at some more.

5
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:47,420
In 1844 French writer Alexandre Dumas wrote The Three Musketeers.

6
00:00:47,960 --> 00:01:00,024
The story is about a young man called D’Artagnan who goes to Paris to join the Musketeers, special soldiers who protect the king.

7
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:12,980
He meets Athos, Aramis and Porthos, three friends who are the greatest Musketeers in France, and they have many adventures together.

8
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:21,680
They often say ‘one for all and all for one’, which shows their strong friendship.

9
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:33,480
The Jungle Book, 1894 by Rudyard Kipling is a story about animals who are very like people.

10
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,210
Some good, some not so good.

11
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:45,420
But there is also Mowgli, a small human boy who grows up in the Indian jungle.

12
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:52,013
Many animals want to find him because he knows how to make fire.

13
00:01:53,220 --> 00:02:08,300
Mowgli’s great friend and guardian is a bear called Baloo and also a black panther called Bagheera, who help him to escape from the tiger, Shere Khan.

14
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:25,800
The Lord of the Rings, 1937 to 1949 by JRR Tolkien is a fantasy story about Frodo who gets a ring from his uncle Bilbo Baggins.

15
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:34,160
Frodo lives in a place called the Shire in Middle Earth and has a friend, Sam.

16
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:45,500
When Frodo leaves the Shire on a long journey with the ring, Sam as well as some other friends goes with him.

17
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:56,959
Sam’s friendship is very important for Frodo as he faces many dangerous situations; Sam is always there to help him.

18
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:07,220
A more modern book is My Brilliant Friend, 2011 by Elena Ferrante.

19
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:12,040
It is the first of a series of four novels.

20
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:17,660
The story begins in Naples in the 1950s.

21
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:24,440
Elena and Lila are friends at school but they have a lot of arguments, too.

22
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:35,600
As they grow up life takes them away from each other, but when they are both old things happen that bring them together again.
